Root cause upstream (yjs/y-webrtc, still unfixed on master as of 2026-09, and
10.3.0 is the latest release): when an 'answer' signal arrives after the local
WebrtcConn was already cleaned up (peer reconnect/room churn), the unguarded
`existingConn.glareToken = undefined` throws a TypeError inside the signaling
message handler, breaking all further signaling on that connection. Guarding
the access is the whole fix; drop this patch once upstream releases one.

diff --git a/node_modules/y-webrtc/dist/y-webrtc.cjs b/node_modules/y-webrtc/dist/y-webrtc.cjs
index 71d0ec4..dcb089c 100644
--- a/node_modules/y-webrtc/dist/y-webrtc.cjs
+++ b/node_modules/y-webrtc/dist/y-webrtc.cjs
@@ -647,7 +647,9 @@ class SignalingConn extends ws.WebsocketClient {
                 if (data.signal.type === 'answer') {
                   log('offer answered by: ', data.from);
                   const existingConn = webrtcConns.get(data.from);
-                  existingConn.glareToken = undefined;
+                  if (existingConn) {
+                    existingConn.glareToken = undefined;
+                  }
                 }
                 if (data.to === peerId) {
                   map.setIfUndefined(webrtcConns, data.from, () => new WebrtcConn(this, false, data.from, room)).peer.signal(data.signal);
